pan>{"01"}</span><strong>{"Measure the waistband, then double it"}</strong></a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-2"}><span>{"02"}</span><strong>{"Measure the seat, under the fly"}</strong></a></li><li data-anim={"fade-up"}><a href={"#step-3"}><span>{"03"}</span><strong>{"Measure the inseam to the hem"}</strong></a></li></ol></div></section><div><nav className={"page-nav"} data-page-nav={""} aria-label={"Article contents"}><div className={"container page-nav-inner"}><a href={"#step-1"} className={"page-nav-link is-active"}>{"01 · Waist"}</a><a href={"#step-2"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"02 · Hip"}</a><a href={"#step-3"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"03 · Inseam"}</a><a href={"#checklist"} className={"page-nav-link"}>{"Before you order"}</a></div></nav><article className={"article-body custom-article py-16 md:py-24"}><p className={"text-xl text-dark"}>{"Most of the jeans that come back to us don’t come back because they’re badly made. They come back because the size on the label meant something different in the last store."}</p><p>{"So we stopped asking people for their size and started asking for three numbers. Take them on the pair of jeans that fits you best, button done up, laid flat on a table. You need a soft tape and ten minutes."}</p><h2 id={"step-1"} className={"page-nav-section"}><span className={"mb-2 block eyebrow font-medium color-primary"}>{"Step 01"}</span>{"Measure the waistband, then double it"}</h2><p>{"Lay the jeans face up and smooth the waistband flat. Measure straight across the top edge, from one side seam to the other, and double the number. That’s your jean size: a 15.5-inch band is a waist 31."}</p><div className={"article-offset"}><figure><div className={"img-frame img-frame-rounded aspect-[4/3]"}><img className={"h-full w-full object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/1200x800.svg"} alt={"Hands measuring the waistband of light-wash jeans with a cloth tape on an oak table"} width={"1200"} heig